# Unity compile self-check

After any C# / Unity script changes in this repo, the agent MUST self-check for compiler errors before considering the task done.

## Required checks

1. Prefer compiling via Unity if available (Editor batchmode / existing MCP compile), **or** at minimum `grep`/read for broken references and run a sanity pass on touched files.
2. On Windows, if `dotnet` or Unity batch compile is available for `Assembly-CSharp`, use it; otherwise carefully verify all referenced symbols exist across partials.
3. Fix CS errors introduced by the change before reporting success.
4. Especially watch **partial class field removals** (`GameUI.*.cs`): renaming or deleting a field in one partial must update every reference in sibling partials (`GameUI.cs`, `GameUI.Interview.cs`, etc.).

## Sanity pass (minimum)

- Grep for the old symbol name after renames/removals.
- Confirm new fields are declared on the same `partial class` and assigned before use.
- Do not report success while known CS0103 / CS0246 / CS1061 remain in touched files.

## Example

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — field removed in GameUI.Interview.cs but still used in GameUI.cs
if (interviewCompanionPortrait != null) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD — all partials use the replacement field
if (interviewPortraitImage != null) { ... }
```
